    <briefdescription>
<para>Conflict Resolution Scenario 3: Callback Under High Churn. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Tests callback invocation and fallback under concurrent updates (&gt;500 ops).</para>
<para><bold>Setup:</bold><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>3-node cluster</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Application callback registered (custom conflict resolver)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>500+ concurrent updates to same model version</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Some updates trigger conflicts</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><bold>Execution:</bold><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Generate 500 concurrent model updates to same version</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Consensus layer detects conflicts (concurrent updates from different nodes)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Invoke callback for each conflict</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Callback returns determistically (based on metadata)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><bold>Verification:</bold><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Callback invoked for each conflict detected</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>All callbacks complete within 5s timeout</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Deterministic outcome: same metadata → same winner</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Conflict resolution latency &lt;50ms (p95)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>No deadlock between consensus and callback</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><bold>Expected P95:</bold> &lt;50ms per conflict resolution </para>
    </detaileddescription>
